From: Lars <118484383+LarzVader@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: aic: allow setting the MAC address

ndo_set_mac_address is only built without CONFIG_AIC8800_STA_ONLY or with
an undefined CONFIG_AIC8800_SUPPORT_REALTIME_CHANGE_MAC, and it is not part
of the regular netdev ops at all. On an AIC8800D80 without a MAC address in
the efuse (Jeazans C107 tablet) the firmware reports a different random
address with the vendor prefix 00:25:92:31 on every boot, so DHCP hands out
a new IPv4 address after each reboot, and user space cannot fix it: setting
a stable address (NetworkManager cloned-mac-address=stable) fails with
EOPNOTSUPP and the connection never activates.

Hook the existing callback up unconditionally. It only works while the
interface is down (eth_mac_addr) and updates wdev.address, which rwnx_open()
passes to the firmware in MM_ADD_IF_REQ, so the firmware uses the new
address from the next open on.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -1201,7 +1201,6 @@
  *	needs to be changed. If this interface is not defined, the
  *	mac address can not be changed.
  */
-#if !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_AIC8800_STA_ONLY) || defined(CONFIG_AIC8800_SUPPORT_REALTIME_CHANGE_MAC)
 static int rwnx_set_mac_address(struct net_device *dev, void *addr)
 {
 	struct sockaddr *sa = addr;
@@ -1218,7 +1217,6 @@
 
 	return ret;
 }
-#endif
 
 static const struct net_device_ops rwnx_netdev_ops = {
 	.ndo_open = rwnx_open,
@@ -1228,9 +1226,7 @@
 #ifndef CONFIG_AIC8800_ONE_TXQ
 	.ndo_select_queue = rwnx_select_queue,
 #endif
-#ifdef CONFIG_AIC8800_SUPPORT_REALTIME_CHANGE_MAC
-	.ndo_set_mac_address = rwnx_set_mac_address
-#endif
+	.ndo_set_mac_address = rwnx_set_mac_address,
 	/* unused interface */
 	//    .ndo_set_features       = rwnx_set_features,
 	//    .ndo_set_rx_mode        = rwnx_set_multicast_list,
